# Line endings, pinned so the frontend quality gate is runnable on Windows.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: `npm run quality:check` runs `prettier --check` first and `ng lint` only if
# it passes. Prettier defaults to `endOfLine: "lf"`, so a working-tree file carrying CRLF fails the
# check on every line - and under `core.autocrlf=true` that is what a Windows checkout produces. The
# committed blobs were always LF and always Prettier-clean; the gate still failed, and because it
# fails at the FIRST half, `ng lint` silently never ran at all.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository AND in the working tree, on every platform,
# regardless of each machine's `core.autocrlf`. That makes the gate mean the same thing everywhere,
# which matters more here than usual: CI gates the deploy on it.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to translate them.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.eot           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.zip           binary
*.dll           binary
